# Step 46c, the diary (diary-lib.el, calendar.el), decided by rule and
# reported in the PR: procedures and commands verb first (R6-17, R6-40),
# a verb taken from what the procedure does where the name has none
# (diary-simple-display displays, diary-sexp-entry processes an entry,
# diary-make-entry inserts an entry string: make_ is for objects in memory),
# append_ for growing an array (one word per meaning: diary-add-to-list),
# plural array names (diary-entries-list), sexp -> expression (term).
# The entry functions of the diary file (diary-date, diary-block,
# diary-float, diary-anniversary, diary-cyclic, diary-offset,
# diary-remind, diary-day-of-year) keep their names, as the forms the
# file names them by; they are private to diary_library_mod.
